* ''The ember's key at rest'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). A separate serving key (SK), the fifth custody class `serving`, wrapped by the vessel key and by ember slots, seals the serving records alone, and the serving tier holds no minting secret: a walker's grant checks under a public half, a shape the hosted road's re-cut lands before the ember's walker arm. An unattended answer (any slot that answers without a person's confirm on the ember) needs a freshness anchor a disk copy cannot carry, a hardware-sealed hearth key whose attestation the ember checks on each ask; without one every ember slot answers only on a person's confirm, threshold two buys a second confirm and never an unattended raise, and after any counted removal a bare deny-only `sk-rotation-owed` mark refuses every ask until SK rolls, a mark a rolled-back disk copy can omit. ''For the operator'': a hearth that holds no hardware anchor raises only on a person's confirm. The reason: a key that opens serving state opens nothing beside it, and a copied disk replays any freshness it carries; the ruling flips on a threat review showing the serving records hold nothing a thief can use even before the grant re-cut (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-table`>>; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ember`>>).

